1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,020
Toon-chan! Toon-chan!

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:23,020
Ah, my fun! Call an ambulance now!

3
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:27,520
I... He didn't have to rush at me like that.

4
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,880
I was only trying to scare you so I could make a point.

5
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,060
Dan-chan!

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Say something!

7
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,900
I'm fine, Mom.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:39,480
You!

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,440
This is your fault!

10
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:43,380
I didn't want all of this to happen!

11
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:44,800
But no!

12
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,720
You just had to keep pushing me!

13
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:57,060
Like with this?

14
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:59,480
I'd kill myself for you!

15
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,280
Meanwhile, you're trying to build a life without me!

16
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,820
You won't even tell me who took the picture!

17
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,240
What?

18
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,340
No one took it!

19
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:09,300
Look!

20
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,480
You can see for yourself!

21
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:11,700
The camera has a timer!

22
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:14,420
And why should I?

23
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:16,820
Everything out of your mouth has been a lie!

24
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:17,640
All of it!

25
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:24,060
There's a timer!

26
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,860
Stop lying!

27
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,080
Right.

28
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,800
Go and get the picture!

29
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,040
I should be trying to save her, not a damn picture!

30
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,260
The cost is too great.

31
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,000
Without that photo, our present is gone.

32
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:49,600
Admit that you've been lying!

33
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,440
Admit that you're trying to replace me!

34
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:55,800
Jiji!

35
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,260
Give that to me!

36
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:58,800
I said give it!

37
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:05,760
You even turned my children against me!

38
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:09,180
Do you have any idea how much I've sacrificed for this family?

39
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:09,680
I'm sorry!

40
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:17,980
I'm sorry.

41
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,200
I couldn't see this coming.

42
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,780
I wouldn't have let you go if I had.

43
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,940
I wouldn't have let you go if I had.

44
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:25,400
I wasn't dunno!

45
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:25,940
She needs help!

46
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,240
God, you're done.

47
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:30,380
I was telling you, I okay...

48
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:53,200
...

49
00:02:54,940 --> 00:03:02,720
In a big, faraway forest, there was a small cabin, and in that cabin lived a family.

50
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:13,180
There was a father, a mother, and a pair of siblings, and they all lived happily together

51
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:14,620
in their forest home.

52
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:24,740
Then, one day, the brother took his sister into the forest to collect berries, and when

53
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:26,640
they were done, night had fallen.

54
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:32,060
They got lost in the dark, and the sister got scared.

55
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:40,660
Then, they came across two crows who could speak, so they asked for directions.

56
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:52,040
But, the crows only laughed at their plight, so the brother, angered by the crows mocking

57
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:57,700
them, killed one with a stone, causing the other to fly away.

58
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:05,580
Brother chased it into the night, and he chased, and he chased.

59
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:11,300
All through the night, he chased, never stopping to rest.

60
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:16,760
That's enough for now.

61
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,100
It's time for bed.

62
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,340
You too, Shishi.

63
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,020
See you tomorrow.

64
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:22,880
Hey, Mom.

65
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,780
Do the siblings in your story ever find their way back home?

66
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:52,560
Had enough?

67
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:53,680
Well, have you?

68
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:53,740
Have you?

69
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,240
Have you?

70
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,740
Have you?

71
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:58,320
Yes, hello?

72
00:04:58,820 --> 00:04:59,900
I need to report a crime.

73
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:02,380
My next-door neighbor is beating his wife.

74
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:06,060
They're at 48 Tongli Lane, room 607 in the Nanda District.

75
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:07,560
You need to send someone now.

76
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,280
I think he's going to kill her.

77
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:14,120
That was your last goddamn mistake, you worthless piece of trash.

78
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:14,960
Get out.

79
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:19,680
I tried to give you a chance, but now you've gone past the point of forgiveness.

80
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:25,260
I'm going to remind you that you're mine.

81
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:29,020
You stupid bitch.

82
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:29,060
You stupid bitch.

83
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,340
Hurry!

84
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:31,380
Hurry!

85
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,180
So, Josh, shut up.

86
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:44,020
What did you learn?

87
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:46,460
What happened?

88
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:48,040
You stopped responding.

89
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:49,880
Don't really know.

90
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:52,120
One minute, everything went black.

91
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,980
Now I'm here.

92
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:54,080
Now I'm here.

93
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,840
That's it.

94
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,100
How is that?

95
00:05:58,520 --> 00:05:59,900
Don't you control when you leave?

96
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,160
Yeah, but I clap like how I go in.

97
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,080
And I might not have.

98
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,120
My last memory doesn't make sense.

99
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:11,260
I was looking at Shishi's dad, but it was like I was in her mother's body.

100
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,300
The rest is blank.

101
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,640
This has never happened before.

102
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,000
It's strange.

103
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,020
Is that it?

104
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,080
What about before?

105
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,380
What did you learn?

106
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:23,960
Anything is helpful.

107
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:26,180
Captain, please be patient.

108
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:27,620
He needs time to recover.

109
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,200
Right, sorry.

110
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:32,080
I'll consolidate everything that we know so far.

111
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:34,300
I'll talk to my people.

112
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,440
Confirm it's her in the photo.

113
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:40,220
The report said she and her husband were both found dead in their apartment.

114
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,820
Their neighbor had called the police.

115
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:47,520
He said they'd been fighting, and he was worried that Li Lan's life was in danger.

116
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,580
They died shortly after the call.

117
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:54,100
Forensics showed that Li Lan killed her husband with a blow to the head from a hammer.

118
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,680
Li Lan died from a stab wound to the abdomen.

119
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:03,620
Their children, Li Tianxian, and his twin sister, Li Tianxie, were found in the apartment.

120
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:07,740
That sounds like what I saw, but it doesn't line up.

121
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:10,920
Li Lan was being abused for years.

122
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,500
Why suddenly fight back?

123
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:13,720
Who knows?

124
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,220
You left right before.

125
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,900
Probably hit a breaking point.

126
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,620
Hey, what about the two children?

127
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:21,580
They knew about the photograph.

128
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,620
Maybe one of them could help us out.

129
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:24,840
That's a dead end.

130
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,620
If we had files, they're gone.

131
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:29,260
They've been ghosts since their parents' deaths.

132
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:29,960
Wait.

133
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,600
There's an informant, but you're the only one they'll talk to.

134
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,040
Says they know the truth.

135
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,240
Me?

136
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,540
Yes, they're waiting for you at the station.

137
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,580
Then let's go.

138
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,800
Hey, wait a second.

139
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,120
Something about this feels off.

140
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,040
You should be careful.

141
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,340
It's a police station.

142
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,340
What could happen?

143
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,320
Don't worry.

144
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:51,100
Chao Ling, keep an eye on him for me.

145
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,200
Just in case.

146
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,820
You need to be careful, too.

147
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,580
The killer is still out there.

148
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,220
There's no telling what he'll do.

149
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,700
I'll arrange for a new guard rotation.

150
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:01,960
Let's go.

151
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:02,300
Hmm?

152
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:06,160
I'll give you a rundown on how to talk to the witness on the ride over to the station.

153
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:06,800
Right.

154
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:17,160
She didn't have anything on her.

155
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,340
Not even a phone.

156
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:21,520
We've been trying to see what we could learn before you arrived.

157
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,060
But she made it clear that she will not talk to anyone unless it's you.

158
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:29,540
She won't remove her mask or let us take anything we could use for a background check.

159
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:33,760
Hell, we had to remove all the monitoring devices in the room before she'd say anything.

160
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:37,740
So don't let her know that you're wired or she'll shut down.

161
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:38,500
Right.

162
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,000
Let's get you bugged, okay?

163
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,420
Shouldn't I have something so I can hear you?

164
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,620
Maybe an earpiece?

165
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,480
That's harder to hide.

166
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,800
And she walked in here not trusting us.

167
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:48,700
I'm sorry.

168
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:49,840
It's too risky.

169
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,980
Just stick to what we covered on the way here.

170
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,480
You set the rhythm.

171
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:57,320
If you do that, you've got control.

172
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,560
You got this.

173
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,840
Now go and crack this case wide open.

174
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:02,060
What all me?

175
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:02,860
Fine.

176
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,000
Fine.

177
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,920
All right.

178
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,320
You got me.

179
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,580
Can I at least know your name?

180
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:22,240
Sure.

181
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:24,780
It's Li Tien-xie.

182
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,520
Li Tien-xie?

183
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,100
It's been a long time coming.

184
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:31,760
Good to meet you.

185
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:39,520
First, get rid of whatever they hit on you.

186
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,220
It can't be.

187
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:46,200
Bring me everything you've found on Li Tien-xie.

188
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:48,120
Everything we have is right here.

189
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:57,260
That's it.

190
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:58,920
There's nothing else on me.

191
00:09:59,400 --> 00:09:59,840
Really?

192
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,560
How considerate of you.

193
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,100
I'd still like to check for myself.

194
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:21,260
All right.

195
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:23,260
All right.

196
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:26,000
Seems like you're trustworthy enough.

197
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:29,380
That's a decent place to start things off, I think.

198
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:34,100
Oh, hey.

199
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:35,820
Can you hold on to this?

200
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:46,600
Now that we trust each other, you mind telling me what you know or why we're meeting at a police station?

201
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,960
Every game has to be a fair give and take.

202
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:49,980
So now I'm giving.

203
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,920
You've played games before, right?

204
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:54,260
It's you.

205
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,860
This will be your punishment for breaking the rules.

206
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:04,440
And now, we get to reset the board.

207
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:07,200
So she's the one who's been controlling people.

208
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,160
But I thought she was mute.

209
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,260
I'm sorry for what happened.

210
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:12,400
I wish...

211
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:12,840
Happened?

212
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,960
How would you know anything that's happened to me?

213
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:18,580
You did flinch when you heard my name.

214
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,240
I see.

215
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,280
You know something at the very least.

216
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,580
Which begs the question.

217
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:27,540
How do you know?

218
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:28,320
Crap.

219
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:32,380
I have no way of knowing if this is Li Tien-xie or if she's possessed.

220
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:38,100
It's too dangerous to mention how I actually learned about what happened.

221
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,180
I'll have to think of how the police might already know.

222
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,760
I said don't lie.

223
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:49,340
Seems your first punishment wasn't enough to get you to stop cheating.

224
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:53,680
See, you can fool me.

225
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,360
But she sees right through you.

226
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,600
No.

227
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,620
I still don't know how she knew I was lying last time.

228
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,420
I can't risk doing it again.

229
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:03,320
Go on then.

230
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:04,940
Don't leave me waiting.

231
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:08,900
I know about your past because of that photograph you gave to us.

232
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:12,300
There.

233
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,840
Isn't the truth refreshing?

234
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:15,500
Speaking of,

235
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,340
this was a big step forward.

236
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:18,620
We should celebrate...

237
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,340
with a soda!

238
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:21,780
Huh?

239
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:22,760
Thanks.

240
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:27,200
Here, I got three cans.

241
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:27,800
Thank you.

242
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,340
I really appreciate this.

243
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:39,340
Is there a way for you to enjoy yourself that's not as disgusting?

244
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,120
That's just what I needed.

245
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:44,760
Soda's the best, isn't it?

246
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,460
Hey, if you don't mind me asking,

247
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:47,840
why do you wear that mask?

248
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:52,720
Ah, look, no judgment.

249
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:53,880
Just curious.

250
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:55,580
It looks uncomfortable,

251
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,540
especially in such a stuffy room.

252
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:58,960
I'm not sick.

253
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,320
I've never been sick.

254
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,100
The world is different for me.

255
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,140
I don't know why,

256
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,440
but since I was a kid,

257
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:11,000
I've always been sensitive to things others aren't.

258
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,700
A light breeze sounds like screaming in my ears.

259
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:16,960
Dog barks are painful.

260
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:19,940
Even a puppy sounds like a roaring monster.

261
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,140
And when people look at me,

262
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,800
it feels like ants are crawling underneath my skin.

263
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,260
I'm always tense.

264
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,500
It kept me from speaking for a long time.

265
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,560
My mom did her best to help me.

266
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,240
That's amazing.

267
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,420
Great job, Shishi.

268
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:40,420
It seemed impossible.

269
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,460
But little by little,

270
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,260
the world stopped hurting so much.

271
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,420
Until that night...

272
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,960
It wouldn't help Shishi anyway.

273
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:49,620
Even if we had the money,

274
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:51,140
she doesn't need a program.

275
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,840
She needs to learn how to be a good wife and mother.

276
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:55,620
Or how not to be one.

277
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:58,020
Hers can't stop batting her eyes at any man

278
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,260
she happens to come across.

279
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:01,820
I lost everything after that.

280
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:04,200
Now the only way I feel safe

281
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,960
is if I cover up as much of my body

282
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,040
as I possibly can.

283
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:10,120
I'm tired of people looking at me

284
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:10,920
and seeing a freak

285
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,500
when I'm just trying to survive.

286
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:15,460
I'm sorry.

287
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,200
I don't think you're a freak.

288
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,160
If you're honestly sorry,

289
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,780
then you should make it up to me.

290
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:23,600
What is it now?

291
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:27,520
The soda went right through her

292
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,920
and now she needs the restroom.

293
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:31,780
Fine, let's go.

294
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,300
About that,

295
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,080
she's still kind of skittish.

296
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:36,260
So yeah,

297
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:37,900
it's best if it's just me.

298
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:44,280
All right, be quick.

299
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:45,380
Go down the hall,

300
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,460
take the first left,

301
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:47,440
then go to the end.

302
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,100
I can show them.

303
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:53,020
Stay with them

304
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:54,440
until they're both back in the room

305
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,860
and keep your guard up.

306
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:57,740
She may try something.

307
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,160
Come on, this way.

308
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:01,200
Come on, this way.

309
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:01,260
Come on.

310
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:11,480
I'll have to go in with you.

311
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,360
Hold on.

312
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:13,740
Do me a favor.

313
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,740
Will you answer my question first?

314
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,080
Yeah, I guess.

315
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:18,360
This can't be everything

316
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,180
we have on them.

317
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,800
There should be a paper trail

318
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,180
documenting what happened to them

319
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:23,280
after the investigation.

320
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:24,360
So where is it?

321
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:25,640
Captain,

322
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,560
I'm worried for Officer Wong.

323
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:28,960
Shouldn't she have some backup?

324
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:29,880
Yeah,

325
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,940
she can handle this herself.

326
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,700
I wouldn't have sent her in alone

327
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:34,720
if I doubted her.

328
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,200
It's just Li Tianxi

329
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,180
is whispering something,

330
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,340
but I can't make it out.

331
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:40,480
I hear it too.

332
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:42,180
I'm sure Officer Wong

333
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:43,020
will fill us in.

334
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:50,900
Jenshin.

335
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:52,900
What?

336
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:58,720
What was that?

337
00:15:58,940 --> 00:15:59,640
Speak up.

338
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:08,480
One more time.

339
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:11,720
I said...

340
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:16,940
Jenshin was Li'd on the case?

341
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:18,100
Captain,

342
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,580
something weird's going on.

343
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:22,140
Damn it.

344
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:23,760
That's no coincidence.

345
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:25,500
The case was the same year

346
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,380
he left the Force.

347
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,380
Hmm.

348
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:27,880
Hmm.

349
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:37,900
You showed up right after

350
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:38,840
we left the room.

351
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,340
And you knew the exact reason

352
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:42,380
why I asked to leave.

353
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,420
So who else is listening,

354
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:44,800
Officer?

355
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,440
Damn it.

356
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:47,580
She caught us.

357
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:48,860
Ugh.

358
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,760
This is my fault.

359
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,220
I sent Wong Juan

360
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:53,200
in way too early.

361
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:55,720
But why tip her hand?

362
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,160
Is she still connected

363
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,460
to Jenshin somehow?

364
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:12,060
Could he be pulling

365
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:13,440
the strings on all of this?

366
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,040
But to what end?

367
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:18,560
Captain,

368
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:19,920
I'm gonna go and check on them.

369
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,220
I'll come too.

370
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:24,340
Hold on.

371
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:30,620
Look, Wong's gone.

372
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:31,620
What happened?

373
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,120
I'm sorry, Captain Xiao.

374
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:34,800
We went inside

375
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,880
and the window was out.

376
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,140
Thought that maybe

377
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:37,900
he had an accident.

378
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:43,880
We've secured the room,

379
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:44,860
but he's not here.

380
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:49,840
Right.

381
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,220
It's time to go.

382
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:59,680
I won't be losing

383
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,380
so easily

384
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,420
this time around.

385
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,040
Officer Wong!

386
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:10,180
Cheng Xiaoshis!

387
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:11,140
You in here?

388
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:15,260
Officer Wong!

389
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:17,340
Cheng Xiaoshis!

390
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:23,760
Captain Xiao,

391
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:24,700
no one's here.

392
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:25,360
They're gone.

393
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,300
It's Wong Juan.

394
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:27,560
She took them.

395
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:28,740
I'm going after her.

396
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:29,960
Officer Wong!

397
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:36,540
What in the world

398
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:37,540
is happening here?

399
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,540
She took them.

400
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,200
But why?

401
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:43,080
It doesn't make sense.

402
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,800
Where would she go?

403
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,560
No time to wonder.

404
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,340
First, we get them back.

405
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,320
Then,

406
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,640
we get some answers.

407
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:50,480
yours.

